sequenceDiagram
    participant Browser as User Browser
    participant GW as Platform Gateway<br/>443/TCP HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    participant KRBP as kube-rbac-proxy<br/>8443/TCP HTTPS TLS
    participant Backend as Dashboard Backend<br/>8080/TCP HTTP (localhost)
    participant GenAI as gen-ai BFF<br/>8143/TCP HTTPS TLS
    participant MaaS as MaaS BFF<br/>8243/TCP HTTPS TLS
    participant K8sAPI as Kubernetes API<br/>6443/TCP HTTPS TLS
    participant LlamaStack as Llama Stack<br/>443/TCP HTTPS TLS 1.3
    participant Thanos as Thanos Querier<br/>9092/TCP HTTPS TLS

    Note over Browser,K8sAPI: Flow 1: User Request → K8s API (Standard CRUD)
    Browser->>GW: HTTPS/443<br/>Auth: OAuth Token
    GW->>KRBP: HTTPS/8443<br/>Token validation
    KRBP->>Backend: HTTP/8080 (localhost)<br/>x-forwarded-access-token
    Backend->>K8sAPI: HTTPS/6443<br/>Auth: Bearer Token (user)
    K8sAPI-->>Backend: JSON response
    Backend-->>KRBP: Response
    KRBP-->>GW: HTTPS response
    GW-->>Browser: JSON response

    Note over Browser,LlamaStack: Flow 2: Module Federation BFF (Sidecar - Gen AI)
    Browser->>GW: HTTPS/443<br/>POST /gen-ai/api/chat
    GW->>KRBP: HTTPS/8443<br/>Token validation
    KRBP->>Backend: HTTP/8080<br/>x-forwarded-access-token
    Backend->>GenAI: HTTPS/8143<br/>x-forwarded-access-token
    GenAI->>LlamaStack: HTTPS/443<br/>Auth: Bearer Token
    LlamaStack-->>GenAI: LLM response
    GenAI-->>Backend: JSON response
    Backend-->>Browser: Streamed response

    Note over GenAI,MaaS: Flow 3: Inter-BFF (Gen-AI → MaaS)
    GenAI->>MaaS: HTTPS/8243<br/>x-forwarded-access-token
    MaaS->>K8sAPI: HTTPS/6443<br/>Bearer Token
    K8sAPI-->>MaaS: Model catalog data
    MaaS-->>GenAI: Model info response

    Note over Browser,K8sAPI: Flow 4: WebSocket Watch
    Browser->>GW: WSS/443<br/>Auth: OAuth Token
    GW->>KRBP: WSS/8443<br/>Token validation
    KRBP->>Backend: WS/8080 (localhost)<br/>x-forwarded-access-token
    Backend->>K8sAPI: WSS/6443<br/>Bearer Token (subprotocol:<br/>base64url.bearer.authorization.k8s.io)
    K8sAPI-->>Backend: Watch events (streaming)
    Backend-->>Browser: WebSocket events
